+### 8.2 Required OpenMA preparation and compatibility
+
+Use the single public `deploy/prepare_openma_source.py` entrypoint, which delegates to `deploy/prepare_openma_deployment.py`. Each stage is source-hash guarded against pinned upstream commit `85d5361f535c7221de975838dc48444e468cc02e`; the complete source maps and composition/runtime identities are recorded in `tank-overlay.json` and `tank-deployment-composition.json`. A partial stage output is not a deployment candidate. Required order and purpose:
+
+| Stage | Required compatibility behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Pinned base/browser/replay/SKILL | PostgreSQL null/bigint representation, opaque custom-tool arguments/configs, browser through SandboxPort, compiled skill manifest, read-only replay-prefix mount and curated credentials; Node24/pnpm and headless console build |
+| `openma_lifecycle` / direct SDK | Declared BoxLite0.10.6 dependency; retain the same native VM/workspace across turns/controller restart, scope/fingerprint guards and SQL fences, idle stop/resume and exact archive cleanup |
+| `openma_execution` | Expose scoped execution IDs/status so Tank waits for actual accepted-input settlement and end-turn rather than HTTP202 or an intermediate idle boundary |
+| `openma_skill_aliases` | Stable `/home/user/.skills/<compiled-name>/` paths for registered skill versions |
+| `openma_file_io` | Bounded binary reads/writes through a process inside the guest so mounted evidence/output permissions apply; no host filesystem bypass |
+| `openma_replay_network` | Replay permits only the resolved private PostgreSQL IP and required native DNS handling, with no internet/provider credentials |
+| `openma_continuation` | Same-session queued custom-tool callback continuation, without creating an arbitrary user turn |
+| `openma_tool_kind` | Registered custom tools keep their custom kind instead of being misrouted as native tools |
+
+The native BoxLite/Go/Rust runtime and sandbox OCI are built separately for `linux/arm64` or `linux/amd64`, using platform-specific pinned downloads, ELF/loader checks and matching OCI architecture. A source rebuild produces `UNQUALIFIED_REBUILD`, never inherited hardware acceptance. Current retained replay-DNS native qualification is ARM-specific; x86-64 deployment requires its own KVM/runtime/browser/network qualification. The setup supports an x86 build path, but does not claim that an ARM binary runs on x86 or that an unperformed x86 hardware test passed. See `deploy/OPENMA_PREPARATION.md` and `deploy/boxlite/v0.10.6/README.md` for exact commands and artifact checks.
+
